G.append({'heading': 'The editor\'s read', 'blocks': [
 p('Three conditions, in the order they resolve. First, today\'s reopen: the hot core print - 0.3% against 0.2% expected - meets Monday\'s nine-month high and its 3.7% PSU bank jump at 9:15 AM, with the ten-year at 5% and GIFT indicating flat; tonight\'s flow print, provisional then confirmed, says whether the foreign tide carried the day or the yield did. Second, the two endgames: oil has priced the Gulf freeze down to an August low without a signed text, and Abu Dhabi\'s second day decides whether "a little bit of flexibility" becomes a framework - Rezaei\'s "no negotiations" and Rubio\'s "blockade is working" are the weights on the other pan; a signed text, a strait schedule, or a resumed strike reprices everything energy touches, ONGC\'s coil first among them. Third, the Wachtell file: the board\'s counsel, the FBI\'s parallel probe, the memo sent earlier this year, and Beijing\'s "smear" line are now one story with a date attached - Nvidia reports 17 November; until the mandate\'s wording surfaces, the market is pricing the man, not the chips. This desk does not predict the answers; it watches these conditions.'),
]})

